From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 03:21:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(kanban-unloaded): gate remote_notices on terminal-row
 prints, reuse swept cards, ignore settled open-chat links

Third cut of t_48c41072e7cba68d. On the hub P1 of #3513 remote_notices ran 21/21 with 0 skips (0.62% of a core):
- the replica token moved on every rewrite of a terminal row (owner bookkeeping) -> now keyed on a per-row notice print
- a ledger commit (the sweep's own observation rows) re-armed the key every run -> not a key component; every probe
  re-judges cards against the ledger
- one settled link in a chat held open by the gateway kept the pass hot -> settled links in open chats are quiet
- cold snapshot (~1.7 s CPU) is cached per replica token so a ledger/live change re-judges without re-reading the replica
---
